A||||6||William Federle||Duke throttle at 80MPH||||1||
Z||000000||William Federle||08-24-2001||07:04 PM||||This morning on the way to work I passed a<BR>car and got up to 80 or 85 MPH. I noticed that as I passed 80 MPH (about 3400 RPM) the car began to accellerate much more quickly than it had been before I got to that speed even though I wasn't pressing the gas pedal at a faster rate.<P>Has anyone else with a 1984 duke observed anything like this? I'm thinking that maybe there is a point in the ECM program where the timing is changed depending on the throttle position sensor and engine RPM.<P>Thanks in advance for replies.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Tigger||08-24-2001||11:56 PM||||4spd or auto?<P>I have an '84 SE with a 4.10 4-speed.  I've noticed it smooths out at around 70-75.  Figure that's a point where the engine and harmonics are well balanced.||||reg||1
Z||000002||artherd||08-25-2001||02:06 PM||||in my 88 V8 I get a nice timing jump (and attendant hp boost) at 3,000rpm :)<P>I'd suspect the same thing you find.<P>It makes my car gobble pavement past 90mph :)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by William Federle:<BR><B>This morning on the way to work I passed a<BR>car and got up to 80 or 85 MPH. I noticed that as I passed 80 MPH (about 3400 RPM) the car began to accellerate much more quickly than it had been before I got to that speed even though I wasn't pressing the gas pedal at a faster rate.<P>Has anyone else with a 1984 duke observed anything like this? I'm thinking that maybe there is a point in the ECM program where the timing is changed depending on the throttle position sensor and engine RPM.<P>Thanks in advance for replies.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
